 #md "# ADR-2606162030: silicon fab brought to runnable cljc + kotoba-Datom

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-06-16
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki

# Context

The silicon actor (珪, ADR-2605242500 + 2605242545) owned the fab-side of the baien
ternary ASICs (iwakura inference / fuigo training). Its physical-design flow is real:
RTL → cocotb → yosys/ABC synth → OpenLane2 sky130 GDSII (DRC/LVS/antenna 0), per
ADR-2605242515 + 2606012800.

But the **fab process** itself had no runnable code. The actor's `cells/*` are langgraph
Pregel scaffolds whose `.solve()` raises `RuntimeError(\"activate via Council ADR\")`, and the
`state_machine.py` per cell only emitted hard-coded mock dictionaries (`mock_deposition`,
`mock_etching`, …) — no process model, no yield, no traceability. The 8 equipment categories
under `50-infra/silicon/equipment/` are README charters.

This left silicon as the **only manufacturing actor with nothing that runs**: niyaku has a
real anti-sway Cartpole sim, giemon/sarutahiko have kami-genesis factory sims. The user
asked to extend the design-implementation to the fab in the same Datomic/Clojure stack the
rest of the roster is migrating onto (ADR-2606160842 py→clj port wave).

# Decision

Implement the fab process as runnable, deterministic **`.cljc` methods** (pure
`clojure.core`, portable, no external deps) under `20-actors/silicon/methods/`, at the same
R0 posture as niyaku: **design + simulation only; live actuation structurally unrepresentable
and Council-gated.**

1. **`fab_flow.cljc`** — the 8-工程 wafer-lot flow
   `litho → deposition → etch → implant → cmp → metrology → test → packaging`. Each step is a
   first-order process-physics model emitting *measured* outputs:
   - litho: Bossung CD `CD = target + k_d·(dose−dose0) + k_f·focus²` (defocus quadratic);
   - deposition: conformal `thickness = rate·time`, rate-dependent uniformity;
   - etch: anisotropic `depth = rate·time`, film-consumption + over-etch penalty;
   - implant: LSS projected range `Rp ≈ a·energy^0.7`, `Rs ∝ 1/dose`;
   - cmp: planarization removal + dishing;
   - metrology: in-line SPC z-gate (non-actuating, adds no defects);
   - test: Poisson wafer-sort yield `Y = exp(−D·A)` over cumulative defect density `D`;
   - packaging: assembly-yield over known-good die.

   Each step contributes to a cumulative defect density that the test step converts to die
   yield — so a recipe excursion (e.g. defocus) measurably lowers yield. **G1 dual-use
   force-review**: a route containing `litho`/`implant` (export-controlled equipment, Charter
   Rider §2(a)(c)) is refused without a `:silen-force-attest`. **G11**: `dispatch-equipment!`
   (real actuation) always raises `:council-gate` — the live-fab boundary is in code.

2. **`wafer_handler.cljc`** — the wafer-handling robotics layer: single-arm cluster-tool
   transfer with a trapezoidal velocity profile, loadlock pump/vent, route cycle-time, and
   bottleneck-bounded throughput (wafers/hr). Plus a **SCARA 2-link forward/inverse
   kinematics + workspace reachability** model — the same PlanarChain topology kami-genesis
   uses (and niyaku's Cartpole port), in pure cljc so it runs in-stack and is testable.

3. **`lot_ledger.cljc`** — **G8 lot traceability**: lowers a completed lot record to
   append-only `:silicon.lot/*` + `:silicon.step/*` EAVT datoms (every measured scalar,
   lossless) and content-addresses them into a sha256 commit-DAG with byte-identical
   canonicalization to `meisai.methods.kotoba`. `verify-chain` is tamper-evident.

4. **`fab_cell.cljc`** — the orchestration \"cell\" (datalog/kotoba): reachability →
   `run-fab-lot` (fab-flow) → `commit-lot` (ledger) → summary, with optional throughput.
   `run-reference` runs the iwakura ternary-PE tile lot on a realistic 8-station layout.

Registered in `bb test:pywasm`; the manifest gains an `:actor/methods` section and a
`fab_flow` datalog cell (`:r0`). The langgraph `cells/*` are left `:pending`/`:r0`
unchanged — not overclaimed.

# Consequences

- silicon now runs end-to-end: **recipe → measured outputs → yield → content-addressed lot
  ledger CID**, at R0 parity with the rest of the manufacturing roster.
- **32 tests / 81 assertions green**; the full `bb test:pywasm` suite stays green
  (676 tests / ~7.5k assertions).
- Honest scope: these are **deterministic first-order models**, not TCAD/foundry-calibrated
  physics. Real equipment RTL/CAD (the 8 `50-infra/silicon/equipment/` categories) and N5
  tape-out remain Phase 2–4 and Council-gated (G11). No constitutional invariant is amended.
- The Datom shape (`:silicon.lot/*`, `:silicon.step/*`) gives danjo/kanae-style observability
  a real lot stream to read when live fab is eventually authorized.

# Alternatives Considered

- **Flip the langgraph cells to runnable.** Rejected: the cells are Pregel/WASM scaffolds
  with a different execution model; the methods layer is the pattern the port wave
  (ADR-2606160842) already uses for niyaku/meisai/etc. Keeping them separate avoids
  overclaiming `.solve()` maturity.
- **Couple to the real kami-genesis Featherstone solver for wafer handling.** Deferred: that
  solver lives in the Rust/Python `nv_compat` layer; a pure-cljc SCARA FK/IK keeps the fab
  in-stack and testable now, and can bridge to kami-genesis later (same way niyaku's
  `isaac_sway_sim.cljc` is a pure-cljc port of the Cartpole).
- **Calibrated process models.** Out of scope for R0; the models are physically grounded but
  illustrative, matching the maturity of the rest of the roster.

